# QUIZFORGE frontend configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust if your backend runs elsewhere.
# No secrets belong in this file.

# --- LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ---------------------------------------------------------
# Leave as-is. The Vite dev server proxies /api to the backend, so the browser
# only ever talks to http://localhost:5173 and CORS is not involved.
VITE_API_BASE=

# --- PRODUCTION (Netlify) -------------------------------------------------------
# Set this in Netlify's build environment (Site settings > Environment variables),
# NOT in a committed file. It is baked into the bundle at BUILD time, so changing
# it requires a new deploy.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE = https://your-backend.onrender.com
#
# Leave it EMPTY to call the same origin (correct when a Netlify proxy redirect
# forwards /api to the backend).
#
# WARNING: never set VITE_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000 for a production build.
# That points the deployed app at the visitor's own machine and every request
# fails with "Couldn't reach the backend".